From 279bfbba83370183e00b19a2006a63e535c72c0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhantao Tang <zhantao.tang@windriver.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Mar 2025 02:25:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] uboot: secure: update secboot codes to compatible with SDK
 BSP43

Since the uboot has been updated to SDK BSP43 release, and the secure
boot flow also changed a lot, so the hse_secboot_enable command should
be modified to keep align with latest status.

And the codes in this commit takes the hse secboot implementation in
pkcs11-hse repo as reference.

The main changes are:
 1. add blx key settings to satisfy new secboot flow
 2. new functions to access and set these new blx keys
 3. add environment variables like blx_pubkey, bl2_bin, bl2_sign to
    specify the resources needed for secboot
 4. new functions to access and set these new environment variables
 5. other settings or changes

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [WR Linux specific]

Signed-off-by: Zhantao Tang <zhantao.tang@windriver.com>
